      "computation_change_reason": "The mandated NOEC statistical method and reference to Part II manuals determine how pass/fail against toxicity limits is computed for A, and which analytical procedure is required for B; ambiguity over 'appropriate method manual' or 'most recent update' could change both the applicable limit comparison and the monitoring method obligation."
    },
    {
      "source": "aztec/final_permit.pdf",
      "locator": "Page: 10, Section: part_i",
      "exact_span": "Dilution water used in the toxicity tests will be receiving water collected as close to the point of discharge as possible but unaffected by the discharge. The permittee shall substitute synthetic dilution water of similar pH, hardness, and alkalinity to the closest downstream perennial water for;\n               i. toxicity tests conducted on effluent discharges to receiving water classified as intermittent streams; and\n              ii. toxicity tests conducted on effluent discharges where no receiving water is available due to zero flow conditions.",
